{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": "Category taxonomy. 'kind' is load-bearing: only kind=expense counts as spending. Transfers (self-transfers, credit-card bill payments, ATM withdrawals, wallet top-ups) and investments are movements of the user's own money, NOT expenses. Counting them is the single most common bug in Indian expense trackers - it is why users see an inflated spend total and stop trusting the app.",
  "kinds": {
    "expense": "Money left the user's net worth. Counts toward spending totals and budgets.",
    "income": "Money entered the user's net worth.",
    "transfer": "Money moved between the user's own accounts (incl. cash). Net zero. Never counted as spend.",
    "investment": "Money moved into an asset the user still owns. Net zero for spend; tracked separately as savings rate."
  },
